radio end-phrase detection: operator said 'that covers it.' then sat through a long silence before resorting to 'i'm done answering the question' — neither is in the soft end-phrase lexicon, so a ~110s capture for a ~30s answer (2026-08-10 hark ask, end_phrase eventually 'over'). Suggest: (1) extend soft utterance-final closers ('that covers it', "i'm done", 'done answering', 'that answers it'); (2) radio idle nudge — after N s of post-speech silence play a soft cue or emit a partial so the agent/ask can offer listen-end; (3) surface partials to blocking ask so it can auto-finish on semantic closers.
